4. `git status --porcelain --ignored; python3 -c "... print(30*86400, 7*86400)"`: exit 0. The test run had left `tests/__pycache__/` and `tinyshop/__pycache__/`. `.claude/` is ignored, was already there, and I didn't touch it.
5. `rm -rf tests/__pycache__ tinyshop/__pycache__ && git status --porcelain`: exit 0. This removed only the caches my runs created, and the tree is clean again.

The commit message says the links will work for a month, but I couldn't run that against real S3. The verdict is FIX until someone runs the S3 check above.

